    {
      "id": 163003,
      "name": "Kratos13",
      "username": "Kratos13",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/k/65b543/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2016-02-19T12:10:38.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Without the fixed seed, the weekly one-shot wouldn't really provide anything new compared to what could already be done: somone posting in the forum about a game setup they played and others trying it out.</p><p>The fixed seed lets everyone try the game with the same starting circumstances so that people can more easily discuss/compare gameplay choices.</p><p>In terms of knowing the deck orders after the first game, well that's what trying to get Mint in your first try is for. &nbsp;And most people avoid reading forum spoilers so they have an honest go at trying for Mint.</p>",
      "post_number": 7,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:43:56.292Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
